# Database Entity Relationship Diagram

```mermaid
erDiagram
    USER ||--o{ PERSON : has
    USER ||--o{ USER_GROUP : belongs_to
    USER ||--o{ USER_ROLE : has
    USER ||--o{ TOKEN : owns

    PERSON ||--o{ ENROLLMENT : has
    PERSON ||--o{ CERTIFICATE : owns
    PERSON ||--o{ NOTE : owns
    PERSON ||--o{ MESSAGE : sends

    COURSE ||--o{ MODULE : contains
    COURSE ||--o{ ENROLLMENT : has
    COURSE ||--o{ CERTIFICATE : issues

    MODULE ||--o{ LESSON : contains
    LESSON ||--o{ ENROLLMENT : tracks

    ENROLLMENT ||--o{ PROGRESS : tracks

    BLOG_POST ||--o{ BLOG_TAG : tagged
    BLOG_POST ||--o{ COMMENT : has

    USER_GROUP ||--o{ USER_ROLE : contains
    USER_ROLE ||--o{ PERMISSION : has

    TOKEN ||--o| TOKEN_USAGE : tracks

    USER {
        int id PK
        string username
        string email
        datetime date_joined
    }

    PERSON {
        int id PK
        int user_id FK
        string first_name
        string last_name
        string phone
        string avatar
    }

    COURSE {
        int id PK
        string title
        string slug
        text description
        datetime created
    }

    ENROLLMENT {
        int id PK
        int user_id FK
        int course_id FK
        string status
        datetime enrolled_at
    }

    CERTIFICATE {
        int id PK
        int user_id FK
        int course_id FK
        string certificate_number
        datetime issued_at
    }

    USER_GROUP {
        int id PK
        string name
        string description
    }

    USER_ROLE {
        int id PK
        int group_id FK
        string name
        string permissions
    }
```

## Key Relationships

- **User → Person**: One-to-One (extended profile)
- **User → Groups/Roles**: Many-to-Many through junction tables
- **Course → Enrollment**: One-to-Many
- **User → Enrollment**: One-to-Many
- **Course → Certificate**: One-to-Many
- **User → Certificate**: One-to-Many
